Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
December 3, 2024
Land Use:Variances/Board App./Plats
17. Presentation by AirLoom Energy on their Low-Cost Turbine
Technology Pilot Project. (No action required)
24 - 564
Presentation, Airloom Energy
Attachments:
Neal Rickner and Heidi Larson, Airloom Energy, explained the project and gave a
presentation. They explained this is an R&D project and a temporary project to test
the physics to prove that the technology works for next-generation wind turbines.
The presentation was received and filed.
18. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a subdivision permit and plat for
Maverick Corner, 2nd Filing, located in a portion of Sect 28, T15N,
R67W of the 6th PM, Laramie County, WY.
24 - 565
Maverick Corner, 2nd Filing, Subdivision Permit and
Plat
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Jones Land Surveying, Inc, on behalf of Chase Lesher,
submitted a subdivision permit and plat application for Maverick Corner, 2nd Filing,
located west of 4922 Klipstein Rd. He said the purpose of the application is to divide
28.18 gross acre parcel into three residential tracts.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval of the
subdivision permit and plat with the adoption of findings of fact a and b with no
conditions.
Acting Chairman Thompson opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no
PUBLIC COMMENT, Acting Chairman Thompson closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to approve the subdivision permit and plat for
Maverick Corner, 2nd Filing, located in a portion of Sect 28, T15N, R67W
of the 6th PM, Laramie County, WY, with no conditions, and adopt the
findings of fact a and b of the staff report.
Commissioner Holmes suggested placing a plat note for no further development on
the remaining 17-acre parcel to ensure compliance with county standards. Acting
Chairman Thompson pointed out that gross acreage of both of the other two tracts is
5.25.
Commissioner Holmes declined to offer an amendment.
The motion carried by the following vote:
Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
Lovett, Malm
Excused:
