### Page 7 of 10

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
December 3, 2024
19. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a zone change from A1 - Agricultural &
Rural Residential to CB - Community Business for Tract 1, Murray Hill
Estates, 7th Filing, Laramie County, WY.
24 - 570
Murray Development, LLC, Zone Change
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said AVI PC, on behalf of Murray Development, LLC,
submitted a zone change application for property in the Murray Hill Estates
Subdivision, 7th Filing, located generally on the southwest side of the I-25 interchange
at Horse Creek Rd. The application asks to rezone the property from A1 - Agricultural
and Rural Residential to CB - Community Business. Arnold said the proposed
rezoning will prepare the parcel for commercial development to align with the County's
Comprehensive Plan.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval of the zone
change with the adoption of findings of fact a and b with no conditions.
Acting Chairman Thompson opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Jessica
Parker, resident, expressed concerns about the aquifer. Hearing no further PUBLIC
COMMENT, Acting Chairman Thompson closed the hearing.
Acting Chairman Thompson spoke about Parker's concerns. He said if there is a
business, a site plan will be needed. He said the site plan would describe the type of
building, landscaping and source of water.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to approve a zone change from A1 to CB for Tract
1, Murray Hill Estates, 7th Filing, Laramie County, WY, and to adopt the
findings of fact a and b of the staff report.
Commissioner Heath said that when the county did the last area planning map, it was
discussed that all the interchanges along interstates would be prime for commercial
development. Commissioner Holmes spoke about the other side of the interstate,
where hours of operation were limited. Commissioner Holmes thanked the developer
for getting the designation on the map so that people who move into the area would
know that it is zoned for commercial enterprise.
The motion carried by the following vote:
Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
Lovett, Malm
Excused:
20. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a vacation and administrative plat for
Archer Estates, 11th Filing, located on the North 1/2 of Tract 9, Archer
Estates, 3rd Filing, Laramie County, WY.
