### Page 8 of 10

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
December 3, 2024
Triple Dot Capital Investments, LLC, Board Approval
Vacation and Administrative Plat, Archer Estates, 11th
Filing
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Steil Surveying Services, LLC, on behalf of Triple Dot
Capital Investments, LLC, submitted an administrative plat application for Archer
Estates, 11th Filing, situated in a portion of the NE1/4 of the SE1/4 of Sect 16, T14N,
R65W, 6th PM, Laramie County, WY. He said the property lies at 12611 Glencoe Dr,
and the purpose of the application is to divide the 10.77 gross acre tract into two
residential tracts. Arnold said Tract 1 will include the existing residence.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval of the
administrative plat with the adoption of findings of fact a and b with no conditions.
Acting Chairman Thompson opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Jessica
Parker, Ann Smith, Richard Wright, residents, expressed concerns about water, lot
sizes, openness, and peace and quiet of country life. Hearing no further PUBLIC
COMMENT, Acting Chairman Thompson closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to approve the administrative plat for Archer
Estates, 11th Filing, located in a portion of the NE1/4 of the SE1/4 of Sect
16, T14N, R65W, of the 6th PM, Laramie County, WY, with no conditions
and adopt the findings of fact a and b of the staff report.
Commissioner Holmes said he is philosophically opposed to going into established
subdivisions with tracts larger than nine acres and splitting them. He expressed
opposition to further subdividing to add another house.
Commissioner Heath said she understands concerns with water and changes in lot
sizes.
Acting Chairman Thompson addressed the public comments. He said he went to the
State Engineer's office to get some scientific basis for determining the minimum lot
sizes for the recharge of the aquifer. He described the process resulting in the AMEC
memo that provided a modeling formula for Laramie County establishing minimum lot
sizes in four different zones based on recharge rates.
Commissioner Holmes said many lots in the area do not meet the 5.25 minimum
acreage standard. He said the overall water usage and the recharge rate in the
densely populated area make it scientifically possible to argue that lot sizes in the
area should be larger than 5.25 acres. Commissioner Holmes felt it was poor policy to
meet the bare minimum requirements for a subdivision or tract.
Commissioner Heath spoke about the need to incorporate recent data from the city of
Cheyenne and get an updated AMEC memo because more water is being drawn
Page 8 of 10
```

### Page 9 of 10

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
December 3, 2024
from the aquifer.
Acting Chairman Thompson reopened the meeting for public comment. Shane
Hansen, Steil Surveying Services, LLC and applicant's agent, pointed out that the
county creates the guidelines, and the applicant has exceeded the minimum
requirements. Hansen said he expected the board to follow its own guidelines.
Acting Chairman Thompson said the AMEC memo provides the scientific formula that
has been the county's policy for the past 10 years. He recommended residents review
the AMEC memo. Acting Chairman Thompson reclosed the public hearing.
Commissioner Holmes recommended postponing the hearing until there is a full
commission. Acting Chairman Thompson noted that an open motion is currently on
the table.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to postpone the hearing until Dec 17, 2024.
Acting Chairman Thompson asked Hansen to comment on the proposed
postponement. Hansen repeated that the applicant exceeds county guidelines. He
said if the application is voted down, a lawsuit may be filed against the county for
going against its own policy. Hansen added he would take on the responsibility of
allowing his client to accept the postponement until the entire board is present.
The motion carried by the following vote:
Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
Heath
Nay:
Lovett, Malm
Excused:
The meeting adjourned at 4:59 pm.
